{"title":"2012 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 3a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> g solution consists of water and salt. 25% of the total mass of the solution is salt. How many grams of water need to be added in order to change the solution so that it is 10% salt by mass?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the total mass of the solution is salt, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31ace96257aefff574ebfc8f98594c3ccbb142b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\% \\times 200 = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 200 = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"214\" height=\"38\" /> grams are salt. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of grams of water that we will add. After we do this, the total amount of grams in the solution would now be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/047b14c293845f3d447d98e0eede46940e3b23d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200 + x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> grams. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the solution is salt but we didn't change the amount from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> grams, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/80276eaf9a70be3d7beaa4aa9185264a3ee157fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\% \\times (200 + x) = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c16193f8cb9488645964c9c4c1c2d80b5f80484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{200 + x}{10} = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/0/5b041dbee886ec8fdc1f75a8bcd5fc17a5a43351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200 + x = 50 \\times 10 = 500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"196\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689817d474d29a2aa0dbb854b061b97d8178c490.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 500 - 200 = \\boxed{300}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"176\" height=\"25\" /> grams\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017230429\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 45/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2047/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.790      1 2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%    5.790      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36054:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017230429 and revision id 279740. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}